      "schema": "attention: choice pytorch, sage, comfy_kitchen = pytorch   # The attention backend. pytorch: ComfyUI's default. sage: SageAttention through KJNodes (needs the sageattention package). comfy_kitchen: ComfyUI's comfy-kitchen kernels.\nsparse_attention: choice none, vsa   # vsa: block-sparse attention (the core Model Sparse Attention node, set up inside H3 Model Optimization). Faster on long or large videos, at some cost in detail. none: full attention.\nspectrum: bool = false   # Spectrum (xmarre's pack): forecasts part of the model's work on some steps instead of computing it. Faster, at a small cost in quality.\nturbo_loader: choice off, normal, larryvrh = off   # How a turbo (few-step) LoRA is applied. off: no turbo LoRA. normal: ComfyUI's LoRA loader, for LoRAs such as LightX2V. larryvrh: Larryvrh's MiniMax-H3 Turbo loader, for its own turbo LoRA.\nsteps: int = 20   # Sampling steps. With a turbo LoRA, the step count it was made for; without one, about 20.\nsampler: @SamplerName (obvpm).sampler_name = euler   # The sampler.\nscheduler: @SchedulerName (obvpm).scheduler = beta   # The noise schedule.\nshift_video: int = 12   # Sigma shift for the video. Higher spends more of the steps at high noise (composition and motion), lower more on fine detail.\nshift_audio: int = 3   # Sigma shift for the audio, like shift_video.\n",
